    "execution": "Set up and position the landmine such that the end is over your toes on one foot.\n\nGrasp the end of the landmine with your hand on the same side as the landmine.\n\nRaise the landmine to a hang position just above your knee. Keep a slight bend in your knee.\n\nSlowly allow the weight to descend by hinging at your hips and allowing your leg opposite the landmine to swing behind you.\n\nMaintain tension in your glutes and hamstrings as you slowly allow the weight to descend.\n\nStop and hold this position for a moment once you feel a light stretch in your hamstring.\n\nEnsure the toes on your back leg are pointed straight down at the floor.\n\nEngage your glutes and hamstrings to drive your hips forwards as you raise the weight back to the starting hang position.\n\nAllow your back leg to swing underneath you.\n\nMaintain good posture by keeping your core engaged for stability and your chest open.\n\nYou should feel this exercise primarily in your glutes and hamstrings, but may notice tension in other areas due to muscular imbalance or restrictions in range of motion.",
