    "execution": "Keep your head straight, look forward and avoid staring down at your feet. Your shoulders should be relaxed.\n\nKeep your arms at a 90 degree angle, and consider swinging them forward and back while running, not across your body. Arm movement helps propel you forward. Relax your hands.\n\nDon’t bend forward or backward from the waist, but rather run in either an upright position or lean forward a bit. Keep your hips stable and forward-facing. Don’t rock the hips from side to side.\n\nDon’t lift the knees to high and land with a slight bend in your knees. Aim to land on the middle of your foot, instead of striking with your heel or forefoot. Make sure your foot strikes under your knee, not in front of it.\n\nBreathe deeply and rhythmically through either your nose or mouth. Avoid shallow or quick breaths.",
