    "execution": "Seat yourself on the bike and adjust the seat height if needed. Position the seat height so your legs are slightly bent during a pedal stroke. Adjust the seat horizontally until the front pedal is directly below your knees.\n\nWhile cycling, position your elbows at a 15% bend and keep your back straight. Hold the handlebars with a light, relaxed grip. As you pedal, don’t sway the bike from side to side. Your knees should track roughly within a line from the hip to the foot.\n\nMake sure your heels are not moving back and forth as you pedal. Overall, pedaling form should be fluid while the body relaxed. A relaxed body absorbs road shock and vibration, whereas a stiff body fatigues from it.\n\nWear protective gear like a helmet to avoid possible injury.",
